1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:01,990
The Science Help Desk is open!

2
00:00:02,390 --> 00:00:03,990
I'm an expert at everything!

3
00:00:04,853 --> 00:00:06,233
Excuse me.

4
00:00:06,613 --> 00:00:10,513
I'm watered every single day, in my beautiful new pot.

5
00:00:10,783 --> 00:00:12,813
So WHY am I wilting?

6
00:00:13,164 --> 00:00:13,894
I know!

7
00:00:14,304 --> 00:00:15,384
You're just feeling...

8
00:00:15,794 --> 00:00:16,464
CHILLI!

9
00:00:16,834 --> 00:00:17,614
Get it?

10
00:00:19,066 --> 00:00:20,706
I've heard that one.

11
00:00:21,053 --> 00:00:23,393
Basil is not an expert at jokes.

12
00:00:24,671 --> 00:00:25,421
Help!

13
00:00:25,711 --> 00:00:26,751
I'm wilting!

14
00:00:27,180 --> 00:00:28,950
Fix one: find out WHY.

15
00:00:29,230 --> 00:00:32,090
Check every part, even the parts we can't see.

16
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:33,600
No time for WHY!

17
00:00:33,970 --> 00:00:35,890
Fix two: MORE WATER, MORE POWER!

18
00:00:36,237 --> 00:00:37,757
Fix three: feed it.

19
00:00:38,197 --> 00:00:39,977
I packed a balanced lunch.

20
00:00:40,326 --> 00:00:41,066
Pip.

21
00:00:41,386 --> 00:00:42,996
Is that MY curry puff?

22
00:00:43,344 --> 00:00:44,734
...It's for science.

23
00:00:45,088 --> 00:00:46,608
Which fix helps Chilli?

24
00:00:46,888 --> 00:00:49,018
Show me one, two or three fingers!

25
00:00:57,636 --> 00:00:59,046
Team high-five!

26
00:01:00,408 --> 00:01:01,568
Let's test them!

27
00:01:01,878 --> 00:01:03,118
Fix two first.

28
00:01:04,170 --> 00:01:05,180
Stand back.

29
00:01:05,470 --> 00:01:07,080
I'm an expert at watering.

30
00:01:08,850 --> 00:01:09,370
Um...

31
00:01:10,270 --> 00:01:10,920
Basil?

32
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:13,290
The water isn't going down.

33
00:01:13,643 --> 00:01:15,123
Because it's SO thirsty!

34
00:01:15,433 --> 00:01:16,253
More!

35
00:01:18,225 --> 00:01:19,175
Blub.

36
00:01:19,595 --> 00:01:21,105
I feel worse.

37
00:01:22,453 --> 00:01:23,063
Look!

38
00:01:23,573 --> 00:01:25,283
The water came out of the top.

39
00:01:25,553 --> 00:01:27,443
But WHY not out of the bottom?

40
00:01:27,792 --> 00:01:29,562
The water is not sinking in.

41
00:01:29,822 --> 00:01:33,562
The soil is already full of water, so more water cannot help.

42
00:01:34,218 --> 00:01:36,458
In my defence, it looked very thirsty.

43
00:01:37,608 --> 00:01:38,738
Fix three.

44
00:01:39,198 --> 00:01:41,708
One curry puff, in four neat pieces.

45
00:01:42,057 --> 00:01:43,067
You made a lunch.

46
00:01:43,427 --> 00:01:44,477
For a plant.

47
00:01:44,831 --> 00:01:46,191
A BALANCED lunch.

48
00:01:49,168 --> 00:01:49,959
Noooo!

49
00:01:50,338 --> 00:01:51,668
My curry puff!

50
00:01:52,022 --> 00:01:52,912
Look, Pip.

51
00:01:53,242 --> 00:01:54,642
You made some new friends.

52
00:01:57,888 --> 00:02:00,478
A plant does not take in food from the soil.

53
00:02:00,778 --> 00:02:03,958
It makes its own food, in its leaves, using light.

54
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:06,480
So the leaves make the food.

55
00:02:06,940 --> 00:02:09,150
My lunch only fed the pigeons.

56
00:02:10,788 --> 00:02:11,938
Look closer.

57
00:02:12,528 --> 00:02:14,348
Momo checks every part.

58
00:02:14,701 --> 00:02:17,061
The leaves are green, so they can make food.

59
00:02:17,331 --> 00:02:18,751
But they're drooping.

60
00:02:19,104 --> 00:02:22,444
The stem should hold the plant upright, so the leaves get light.

61
00:02:22,684 --> 00:02:24,304
This one is bending.

62
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:26,730
Now somebody has to feel the soil.

63
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:27,990
Not Pip.

64
00:02:28,230 --> 00:02:30,020
Pip is scared of mushy things.

65
00:02:30,369 --> 00:02:31,239
I am.

66
00:02:31,779 --> 00:02:33,439
But Chilli needs help.

67
00:02:35,017 --> 00:02:35,957
Chilli?!

68
00:02:35,993 --> 00:02:37,603
That was the SOIL!

69
00:02:37,952 --> 00:02:39,422
It really was the soil.

70
00:02:39,692 --> 00:02:41,742
Soil this soggy is full of water.

71
00:02:44,917 --> 00:02:46,797
The roots are brown and mushy!

72
00:02:47,087 --> 00:02:49,807
And there's no hole at the bottom, so the water had nowhere

73
00:02:49,827 --> 00:02:50,667
to go!

74
00:02:51,244 --> 00:02:51,924
Pong!

75
00:02:52,254 --> 00:02:53,434
That's not a smell.

76
00:02:53,744 --> 00:02:54,884
That's a clue.

77
00:02:55,925 --> 00:02:56,665
Wait.

78
00:02:56,925 --> 00:02:58,475
Chilli has loads of water.

79
00:02:58,875 --> 00:03:00,275
So why is it droopy?

80
00:03:03,125 --> 00:03:04,625
Roots need air, too.

81
00:03:05,225 --> 00:03:08,655
In soil this wet, the spaces between the bits of soil are

82
00:03:08,675 --> 00:03:11,455
filled with water, so there is no air.

83
00:03:12,025 --> 00:03:14,735
The roots go soft and brown, and rot.

84
00:03:15,462 --> 00:03:19,252
Rotting roots cannot take in water, so the leaves droop, even in

85
00:03:19,272 --> 00:03:20,212
wet soil.

86
00:03:20,948 --> 00:03:24,478
Healthy roots absorb water and mineral salts from the soil.

87
00:03:24,728 --> 00:03:26,648
To absorb means to take in.

88
00:03:26,948 --> 00:03:28,528
Chilli's roots couldn't.

89
00:03:29,099 --> 00:03:30,209
Sorry, Chilli.

90
00:03:30,499 --> 00:03:32,319
My extra water made it worse.

91
00:03:32,667 --> 00:03:34,247
You were trying to help.

92
00:03:35,395 --> 00:03:37,475
So the roots couldn't absorb water...

93
00:03:37,539 --> 00:03:39,919
...so the stem had no water to carry up...

94
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:41,340
...so the leaves drooped!

95
00:03:41,630 --> 00:03:43,030
The plant is a system.

96
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:46,670
One part stopped working, and the whole plant was affected!

97
00:03:48,282 --> 00:03:49,922
Seven o'clock.

98
00:03:50,172 --> 00:03:51,712
Watering time!

99
00:03:52,022 --> 00:03:55,822
One jug, every day, for maximum efficiency.

100
00:03:56,169 --> 00:03:56,919
Wait.

101
00:03:57,189 --> 00:03:58,859
YOU water Chilli every day?

102
00:03:59,208 --> 00:04:00,248
Correct.

103
00:04:00,578 --> 00:04:02,598
I also chose this pot.

104
00:04:02,838 --> 00:04:05,778
No holes, so no water is wasted.

105
00:04:06,128 --> 00:04:07,748
He's me, ten minutes ago.

106
00:04:08,099 --> 00:04:12,359
Um... the water had nowhere to go, so the roots got no air.

107
00:04:12,855 --> 00:04:14,185
Incorrect.

108
00:04:14,435 --> 00:04:15,955
Show me the data.

109
00:04:18,527 --> 00:04:22,017
Brown, mushy roots, and a pool of water with no way out.

110
00:04:23,388 --> 00:04:24,058
Error.

111
00:04:24,628 --> 00:04:26,218
My plan was...

112
00:04:26,468 --> 00:04:27,978
not efficient.

113
00:04:28,329 --> 00:04:29,969
You wanted to help Chilli.

114
00:04:30,269 --> 00:04:31,329
So did we.

115
00:04:31,659 --> 00:04:33,249
Let's fix it together.

116
00:04:33,604 --> 00:04:34,664
Updating!

117
00:04:35,034 --> 00:04:37,654
Lesson stored: roots need air.

118
00:04:38,064 --> 00:04:40,474
Drainage holes: required.

119
00:04:41,930 --> 00:04:44,900
We need holes in the bottom, so the extra water can drain

120
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:45,610
out.

121
00:04:45,959 --> 00:04:48,769
And an adult must cut off the rotting roots, and add fresh

122
00:04:48,789 --> 00:04:49,609
soil.

123
00:04:50,108 --> 00:04:50,998
Aiyoh.

124
00:04:51,288 --> 00:04:52,928
Uncle can help.

125
00:04:53,282 --> 00:04:55,742
Could everybody turn around, please?

126
00:04:58,510 --> 00:05:00,760
Okay, can look already.

127
00:05:01,108 --> 00:05:02,418
Now the water test.

128
00:05:04,795 --> 00:05:05,755
It drains!

129
00:05:06,035 --> 00:05:07,815
The water has somewhere to go now!

130
00:05:08,168 --> 00:05:11,958
New rule saved: water only when the top of the soil is

131
00:05:11,978 --> 00:05:12,848
dry!

132
00:05:14,831 --> 00:05:16,691
Slowly, slowly lah.

133
00:05:17,021 --> 00:05:18,931
Plants cannot rush one.

134
00:05:19,472 --> 00:05:20,682
Two weeks later...

135
00:05:23,854 --> 00:05:25,774
I'm standing tall again!

136
00:05:26,224 --> 00:05:28,014
Thank you for listening.

137
00:05:28,454 --> 00:05:31,054
Nobody ever listens to a plant.

138
00:05:31,408 --> 00:05:32,668
I know the feeling.

139
00:05:32,939 --> 00:05:34,999
Be a drop of water in Chilli's pot!

140
00:05:35,279 --> 00:05:36,269
Shrink down.

141
00:05:36,549 --> 00:05:37,479
Quietly.

142
00:05:39,043 --> 00:05:42,633
You trickle down through the soil, past little pockets of air.

143
00:05:43,413 --> 00:05:45,613
Some mineral salts come along with you.

144
00:05:45,753 --> 00:05:47,723
A firm white root takes you in.

145
00:05:48,503 --> 00:05:50,053
You're inside the plant!

146
00:05:50,185 --> 00:05:53,185
Up you go, through the stem, all the way to a leaf,

147
00:05:53,205 --> 00:05:54,485
where food is made.

148
00:05:55,973 --> 00:05:59,253
So the stem carries water and mineral salts up, and food from

149
00:05:59,273 --> 00:06:01,033
the leaves to other parts.

150
00:06:01,523 --> 00:06:03,133
The stem transports them!

151
00:06:04,992 --> 00:06:07,392
Now, here are the words that earn marks.

152
00:06:07,449 --> 00:06:08,749
Say it with me!

153
00:06:09,459 --> 00:06:12,659
The roots hold the plant firmly in the soil and absorb water

154
00:06:12,679 --> 00:06:14,229
and mineral salts.

155
00:06:14,489 --> 00:06:18,689
The stem holds the plant upright and transports water, mineral salts and

156
00:06:18,709 --> 00:06:20,739
food to all parts of the plant.

157
00:06:20,949 --> 00:06:22,969
The leaves make food for the plant.

158
00:06:23,189 --> 00:06:24,749
A plant is a system.

159
00:06:25,089 --> 00:06:28,319
When one part stops working, the whole plant is likely to be

160
00:06:28,339 --> 00:06:29,259
affected.

161
00:06:31,957 --> 00:06:33,597
Seven o'clock.

162
00:06:33,877 --> 00:06:35,827
A little top-up, Chilli?

163
00:06:36,179 --> 00:06:38,459
Is the top of my soil dry?

164
00:06:38,845 --> 00:06:39,795
...No.

165
00:06:40,081 --> 00:06:41,381
Then, no.

166
00:06:41,618 --> 00:06:43,158
Rule saved.

167
00:06:46,104 --> 00:06:47,274
Picked fix one?

168
00:06:47,544 --> 00:06:49,594
You win a point, and so does Momo!

169
00:06:51,380 --> 00:06:52,570
A mystery leaf!

170
00:06:52,850 --> 00:06:55,000
Next time, we open a case file.

171
00:06:55,588 --> 00:06:57,788
Let's read today's key words together!

172
00:06:58,078 --> 00:06:58,838
Ready?

173
00:06:59,125 --> 00:07:00,155
Make food.

174
00:07:01,645 --> 00:07:02,565
Absorb.

175
00:07:04,027 --> 00:07:05,027
Transport.

176
00:07:06,502 --> 00:07:07,442
Well done!

177
00:07:08,424 --> 00:07:09,525
Say it with us!

178
00:07:10,326 --> 00:07:11,076
Ready?

179
00:07:11,199 --> 00:07:11,859
One!

180
00:07:12,199 --> 00:07:12,899
two!

181
00:07:13,204 --> 00:07:14,379
Now you know!

182
00:07:19,389 --> 00:07:21,329
Fix two: MORE WATER, MORE POW...

183
00:07:22,303 --> 00:07:24,215
Now YOU'RE the droopy one.

184
00:07:24,235 --> 00:07:24,985
Towel?

185
00:07:25,545 --> 00:07:26,685
Take two!

186
00:07:30,568 --> 00:07:32,928
New knowledge acquired.
